        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): bound conflict-marker scan reads to prevent OOM on large files",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`pnpm check:no-conflict-markers` previously read every candidate tracked file returned by `git grep` into memory whole via `fs.readFileSync`. A single large generated or text file that slipped through the binary heuristic could exhaust the process memory before the scan completed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Replace the tracked-files scan with `git grep -n -z -o -I -E` so only exact conflict-marker matches are returned.\n- Parse the grep output (path, line number, match) into violation records without buffering file contents.\n- Keep `findConflictMarkersInFiles` for direct, small-scale use; the tracked-files path no longer reads files whole.\n- `findConflictMarkersInTrackedFiles` now returns paths relative to the repository root, matching `git grep` output.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Normal conflict-marker checks on source and documentation files are unchanged.\n- Oversized or generated files can no longer cause an OOM during the scan because their contents are never read.\n- CI and pre-commit runs remain robust against accidental large-file commits.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal focused test passes:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.test.ts --run\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\n✓ |tooling| test/scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.test.ts (9 tests) 585ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  9 passed (9)\n```\n\nAdded regression tests covering:\n- tracked files with conflict markers reported via `git grep`\n- clean tracked files returning no violations\n- binary tracked files skipped by `git grep -I`\n- paths containing spaces and unusual characters\n- large files whose line numbers are reported without reading the whole file\n- `main()` printing paths relative to the repository root\n\nRebased onto current `upstream/main` to pick up the independent `scripts/lib/sqlite-reliability-runner.ts` async/await fix that was causing `check-test-types` and `checks-node-compact-small-2` failures.",
        "branch": "fix/scripts-bound-conflict-marker-scan",
